 ## Version log
 
+### 2026-08-29, The improvement-plan batch ran: six stages, and a 44% spread on the boat that every gate accepted (branch `OSP-boat-count-incorporation`)
+
+`06_diagnostics/run_improvement_plan_2026-08-27.R` completed all six stages (~22 h). Every question it asked got an answer, and the answers together exposed a larger one. Full review in `development_notes/improvement-batch-review-2026-08-29.md`; follow-up work in Stage 5 of `improvement-plan-2026-08-27.md`.
+
+-   **THE HEADLINE. The private-boat all-gear estimate ranges over 25,883 to 37,392 across six configurations that ALL pass the convergence gate**, an 18% spread at the port total (66,237 to 78,250). Every one of those fits has R-hat under 1.01, n_eff over 400, a divergence fraction under 5% and impact under 0.10 SD. For scale, the entire 2026-08-25 improvement batch moved the port total 1.6%. The gate tests whether a fit sampled, not whether the model is right, and was never designed to do the latter. Any external presentation of the boat number now has to name the configuration that produced it.
+-   **Stage D, the gate: PASSED.** `shared_tau = FALSE` reproduces rung 4 with 11,217 shared parameter rows identical at full double precision and a byte-identical `convergence_report.csv`, so stage E is attributable to the feature.
+-   **Stage E, shared turnover: the boat turnover moves, with unusually good corroboration.** `tau_bar` = 2.597 [2.064, 3.249] against a prior centred on 1.20. Four independent lines agree: the OSP/trailer overlap calibration implies 2.01-3.03; the trailer and OSP PIT means converge on 0.50 simultaneously and in opposite directions (bias down 81% and 73%); boat trailer `elpd_loo` gains +14.67 at paired z = +2.66 with `p_loo` staying low; and convergence improved (divergences 97 -> 39). Boat all-gear 25,883 -> 31,012. Qualifications: the posterior sits above the prior's 95% envelope so 2.597 is shrunk, and `n_ie_obs = 0` for this fit, so the turnover is identified indirectly through the count streams and must never be called measured.
+-   **Stage E's SHORE result must not be carried forward.** Shore all-gear moved +17.9% on its own `tau_bar` (1.700 -> 2.080), backed by 4 of 289 informed days, with an interval that still contains the 1.7 prior centre, no measurable improvement in fit, and no replication in the gear track (which put the same parameter at 1.681). The toggle is global and needs an informed-day floor.
+-   **Stage B, reseeded rung 2: seed-dependent, but the configuration is marginal.** The fit survived (488 divergences, 4.88% against a 5% backstop, worst chain 350, `E_sum` n_eff 924 against the shipped config's 5,914). Two seeds, two struggling chains. The I/E unit fix alone does strain the shore all-gear daily fit; the weekend fix is what makes the shipped configuration comfortable. The clean isolation now confirms the I/E result three ways: `sigma_IE` 0.238 / 0.300 / 0.272 against 1.068 before the fix.
+-   **Stage C: the 13% cross-track gap on the boat pot closure was a configuration artefact.** Forced to biweekly the pooled fit gives 735 against the gear track's 743. The run was contaminated by an `ar_force` defect found in this review (see below), so its port total is not interpretable; the pot-closure conclusion stands.
+-   **Stage F, the escalation ladder: every component passes at DAILY on the first attempt, and the daily boat fit is absorbing rather than identifying.** Shore pot closure at daily gives 111 divergences where Run 6 recorded 1,165, so the funnel that justified the biweekly cap is gone and `ar_max_resolution` is now the only thing holding production coarse. But the boat at daily raises catch 44% while `p_loo` on the trailer stream goes 4.9 -> 31.8 with 2 bad Pareto k, the CATCH stream's elpd gets WORSE, and `r_OSP` collapses 1.62 -> 10.61 with a 95% upper bound of 1,405 (its parent `sigma_r_OSP` at n_eff 307, below the gate's own floor on a parameter the gate does not check). The entire increase lands in the extrapolated portion.
+-   **Stage A, empty-stratum fill: `day_type` raises every affected component's PE 20-27%**, about 13% at the port level. The `zero` fill has been biasing the PE down by roughly an eighth, which matters for the PE-vs-BSS cross-check and for any component that falls back to PE.
+-   **Two defects found and fixed.** `ar_force` was per-population only while `ar_max_resolution` had gained the nested per-sub-season form, and `as.character()` on a one-element list returns its element, so a nested `ar_force` silently forced every sub-season of that population; that is what contaminated stage C, moving boat all-gear 25,883 -> 28,902 as a side effect. It now takes the same shapes as `ar_max_resolution` and errors on an unnamed list. Separately, stage A did not load the crabbing-holiday workbook the way the driver does, so its stratification (85 cells) and zeroed-day counts (41/44/8/0) did not match the driver's (92 cells, 44/47/9/0); the comparison was still fair because both arms shared the stratification.
+-   **No configuration change is adopted.** The shipped rung-4 configuration stands as authoritative. Stage E is the strongest candidate to change it and should not be adopted on one pooled run with a failed gear cross-check and a shore side effect that has to be suppressed first.
+-   Harness at **128 assertions**. Files changed: `03_R_functions/bss_ar_resolution.R`; `06_diagnostics/run_improvement_plan_2026-08-27.R`, `test_improvements_2026-08-25.R`; `development_notes/PIPELINE_STATUS.md`, `improvement-plan-2026-08-27.md`, new `improvement-batch-review-2026-08-29.md`; this history.
+
 ### 2026-08-27b, Shared-turnover parameterization, the OSP predictive check, and the improvement-plan batch (branch `OSP-boat-count-incorporation`)
 
 Makes the improvement plan runnable. The model change is the substantive part; everything else is plumbing for it.
